Ocean module — third-party attribution
=======================================

The wave spectrum and the FFT in this Ocean module are ported from Crest's
FFTSpectrum.compute, FFTCompute.compute and OceanWaveSpectrum under the MIT
License (the ocean_fft_* shaders in Engine/Modules/Rendering/Shaders/Ocean).
The foam and water-shading algorithms are engine-native implementations whose
behavior is modeled on the Crest ocean system by Wave Harmonic. The concentric
patch types, patch placement, checkerboard triangulation, grid snapping, and
smooth LOD-transition logic in the ocean surface mesh are adapted from Crest's
OceanBuilder and OceanVertHelpers under the MIT License. Foam2.png and
WaveNormals.png from the same pinned source are included as crest_foam.png and
crest_wave_normals.png in Apps/Editor/Assets/Examples/Materials/Ocean. The foam
relief, bubble parallax, and two-phase flow sampling in ocean_surface.glsl are
adapted from Crest's OceanFoam.hlsl and OceanNormalMapping.hlsl under MIT. A
copy of the license accompanies the example textures.

The temporal hard/soft shadow fields and continuous spline ribbon input model
follow Crest's LodDataMgrShadow and spline-input concepts. Their render-graph,
CSM, tile-binning, underwater BVH, per-body material, and GPU spray integrations
are engine-native implementations.

Reference (algorithmic source):

- Repository: https://github.com/wave-harmonic/crest
